            "review_title": "Review at Grand Palace",
            "review_text": "Adrian N\n16 contributions\n0\nVery good, but needs a bit more personal touch\nNov 2017 • Family\nThis hotel is very good. If staying try for a room in the old part, near the pool. It's architecture is a welcome respite from siagons newness. The roof top bar is ideal an evening drink and breakfast is very good. \nThe reason I'm not giving it excellent is that having stayed in a supposed lower grade hotel in Hanoi, it set the bench mark for the Grand. The Grand needs a little more personal touch to be truly a five star in my opinion, that said I would recommend it.\nRead more\nWritten November 13, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
