            "review_title": "Review at Grand Palace",
            "review_text": "tkzrea\n114 contributions\n0\nNice and cozy restaurant to start your day\nMar 2016 • Couples\nAs part of the Grand Saigon hotel package, we had breakfast included with out stay. They restaurant is very nicely laid out with the Buffett arrangements in a wide spread area which does not cause overcrowding.\n\nThe breakfast selection was also nicely prepared. There was egg and noodles section, Japanese, Chinese and the local breakfast was served in a nicely spaces area. The continental breakfast selection with is nicely done croissant was really a pleasant. However, the best for me was the fruit selection and the freshly squeezed juice, especially watermelon which is not common in most restaurants.\n\nIn terms of service, the staff were very helpful and friendly. Service was quick and therefore you can get you table cleared very quickly enough without worrying that you won't have space to go for a second or third helping. The view of the internal garden was also refreshing in the early morning.\nRead more\nWritten March 5, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
